{"title":"2022 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Regular pentagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> is inscribed in circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />are th with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/c/66c98fae1403b2e04e000b76895df336b8522dde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. Circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> is the reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> across <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f32db217d7630882c3441fa8821cd70a6958c3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be an intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1a61b7cccb5fc02c843c7b58e2d671c4c2c6d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DO}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />, and let line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> be the tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. The sum of the possible distances from point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2f1dcbb9badfd3447d4e7351678b7d71ea9bff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\sqrt{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"21\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a squarefree positive integer. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a39dfbb882af1dee503f5b4bb3a4aac93ab473d9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(8cm); pair O = (0,0); pair O_ = (0,(sqrt(5)+1)/2); pair A = dir(54); pair B = dir(126); pair C = dir(198); pair D = dir(270); pair E = dir(342); pair I = ((sqrt(5)-1)*sqrt(10-2*sqrt(5))/8,(sqrt(5)-2)/2);  draw(A--B--C--D--E--cycle); draw(circle(O,1)); draw(arc(O_,1,210,330),blue); draw(A--D,magenta); draw(B--E,magenta); draw(D--(0,1.25),dashed+red);  dot(&quot;$O$&quot;,O,E); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,2*dir(10)); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,2*dir(170)); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SW); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,S); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,SE); dot(&quot;$I$&quot;,I,dir(30)); [/asy]\" width=\"345\" height=\"378\" /> </center><p> Position <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is horizontal. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/f/7ff1d53900652da5f2d40ef5427512642e85c0b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DO$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> is vertical, and it follows that both positions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> are horizontal. Scaling down by a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/c/66c98fae1403b2e04e000b76895df336b8522dde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> to the unit circle, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/7/c67d1bdb99bcc54798d9853fbfd10aa5085d03f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(54)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />. So, the two positions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordiantes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/9/fd9bad0aef18de62065597c8d758195fa888f683.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sin(54)-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9b2931e0da2c441c4b7d6e2b73c1ffe67bbf539.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sin(54)+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"20\" />. Now, we use complex numbers to find the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa0cef545bc24bb364e2f57af2b61b111b670151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega=e^{\\frac{\\pi i}{10}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"19\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/7091050d2489f4a190a810efdca21ada55f5fae9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=\\omega^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/3/e93e7a38f2dc23e42207231279399a6c82b7a0ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=\\omega^7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/2/06272ad971fc9aece8fb796018a1a1800e32446c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=\\omega^{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/a/3fa6eccc24e95541d784e8aeeb63e891f5055604.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=\\omega^{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"17\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/6/d3663791bfc41f9d4a88490d61540a1c44f999c0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[I=\\frac{\\omega^3\\omega^{15}(\\omega^7+\\omega^{19})-\\omega^7\\omega^{19}(\\omega^3+\\omega^{15})}{\\omega^3\\omega^{15}-\\omega^7\\omega^{19}}=\\omega^7(1-\\omega^4+\\omega^8).\\]\" width=\"467\" height=\"39\" /> So, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/7/f17295cde9a66f0b2b672085341b814fa245fb1c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(7\\cdot18)-\\sin(11\\cdot18)+\\sin(15\\cdot18)=\\sin(54)+\\sin(18)-1.\\]\" width=\"483\" height=\"18\" /> The sum of the two possible distances is  \\begin{align*} &amp;\\quad\\left((2\\sin(54)-1)-(\\sin(54)+\\sin(18)-1)\\right)\\\\ &amp;+\\left((2\\sin(54)+1)-(\\sin(54)+\\sin(18)-1)\\right)\\\\ &amp;=2(\\sin(54)-\\sin(18))+2=3. \\end{align*} Scaling back up, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e74de1ad70a474ace4849e62faf97d601fc1b34.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5\\sqrt{5}\\cdot3=15\\sqrt{5}\\implies 15+5=\\boxed{20}.\\]\" width=\"278\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018022215\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.063 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 185/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8810/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26212:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018022215 and revision id 280172. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}